{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>I said</b>. He speaks to his soul regarding the essence of merriment." "<b>Come now, I will test with joy</b>. If wisdom produces anger, I will abandon it and turn to engage in matters of joy and to mix wine, as in the phrase 'and they drank wine, mixed' [Proverbs 23:30]. And if they are two roots, and it is from the dagesh construction, like אדברה / וינסך, like וידבר. And there are those who say it is from נסה, and the kaf is to liken the addressee, as in אנסה אותך, like אחוך, 'hear me,' אכנך, 'and you did not know me.'"], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The last example phrase 'שמע לי אכנך ולא ידעתני' appears to concatenate several scriptural allusions; rendered hyper-literally as the sense-unit stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:10.439457023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}